    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE DIRECTION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WAVE DIRECTION</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 09:00 AM EDT<br/><b>Source updated:</b> n/a (NOMADS)<br/><b>Source version:</b> glwu-20260925-1300Z-wvdir<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-25 01:32 PM EDT<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis), 6-hourly cycles</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_direction/legend.png?v=glwu-20260925-1300Z-wvdir" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Wave direction (compass degrees, as filed by GLWU WVDIR): <b>LOWEST 0 N</b> dark-blue &rarr; <b>45 NE</b> cyan &rarr; <b>90 E</b> green &rarr; <b>135 SE</b> yellow &rarr; <b>180 S</b> orange &rarr; <b>225 SW</b> red &rarr; <b>270 W</b> magenta &rarr; <b>315 NW</b> violet &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 360 N</b> dark-purple (wrap: both ends northerly). Same degree always shows the same color. Arrows point where the waves are traveling (filed direction + 180&deg;). Lake mean now: <b>134&deg; (SE)</b>.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — WVDIR surface analysis<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20260925/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t13z.grib2">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20260925/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t13z.grib2</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE WAVE DIRECTION</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WAVE DIRECTION</h2><p>Mean wave direction on the lakes right now, in compass degrees exactly as filed by the NOAA wave model. Color tells direction at a glance; arrows show which way the waves are traveling.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_direction/legend.png?v=glwu-20260925-1300Z-wvdir" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Wave direction (compass degrees, as filed by GLWU WVDIR): <b>LOWEST 0 N</b> dark-blue &rarr; <b>45 NE</b> cyan &rarr; <b>90 E</b> green &rarr; <b>135 SE</b> yellow &rarr; <b>180 S</b> orange &rarr; <b>225 SW</b> red &rarr; <b>270 W</b> magenta &rarr; <b>315 NW</b> violet &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 360 N</b> dark-purple (wrap: both ends northerly). Same degree always shows the same color. Arrows point where the waves are traveling (filed direction + 180&deg;). Lake mean now: <b>134&deg; (SE)</b>.</p><p><b>Units:</b> degrees (compass: 0/360=N, 90=E, 180=S, 270=W)<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — WVDIR surface analysis<br/><b>Update:</b> GLWU 6-hourly cycles (analysis step)<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 09:00 AM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> glwu-20260925-1300Z-wvdir<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-25 01:32 PM EDT<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/cgi-bin/filter_glwu.pl">NOMADS GLWU</a></p>]]></description>
